-- Source module: Solutions.J6SegAxA4
/-!
# `A`-line axis program (`AxisUA6`), part 4: the eight-step chain of `pipeAL`

The `A` per-axis pipeline `J6A.pipeAL p s t α H pre post` (`J6AIL6`) is the composition of
eight one-array steps (`M = t / 16H`, `2^f = 8H`, `N = pre · t · post`):

1. `dupL 32` (the copies),           2. `blkT 2^5 N 1` (fine exposure, forward),
3. `blkT (t·post) 2^5 pre` (back),   4. the gather slab pass (`srcG`),
5. `blkT 2^3 (M·8H·post) pre`,       6. `blkT (8H·post) 2^3 (pre·M)` (`rgp`),
7. the kernel pass `kerPass 2^f post (pre·8M) (gK ∘ (· % 8M))`,
8. the compress slab pass (`srcC`).

**`axA_chain`**: `PassOK` steps for these maps (with their natural preconditions: the length,
`GB w` before the kernel, `GB w'` after it) compose to a `PassOK` step for `pipeAL` with the
precondition `|L| = N ∧ GB w L`.
Also the value-bound helpers `GB_dupL`, `GB_blkTg`, `GB_lineAt`, `GB_of_LRep`, `GB_slabId`.
-/

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false

noncomputable section

namespace J6Seg.Ax
open IntMul NLogN NLogN.KIL NLogN.KFB IntMul.Kappa.R6 Function

/-! ## Value bounds through the list passes -/

/-! ## Weakening a step -/

/-! ## The chain -/

/-- The eight-step program. -/
def axAProg {Pp : ℕ} (st1 st2 st3 st4 st5 st6 st7 st8 : IStmt HS Pp) : IStmt HS Pp :=
  .seq st1 (.seq st2 (.seq st3 (.seq st4 (.seq st5 (.seq st6 (.seq st7 st8))))))

end J6Seg.Ax

end

