# Side costs 5: **`sideCost6_all`**

Against `cU6 P n 2 = T p · Ncost6 · (log lg n + 1)^2` with `Ncost6 ≥ d + ℓ`, `d = D + 1`:
every side cost is `≤ Kc · cU6 P n 2 / (D + 1)` with
`Kc = 10^12 (W+15)^3 (W+x+14)^2 (Cfm+1)`, `W = 3 wA + wC`.
